course: dictionary
lesson: 15098
title: Routinely: how often things happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Routinely comes from routine, a thing you do the same way again and again. It means something happens as a normal, regular part of life, or usually. «Mum routinely packs my lunch on school days.» She does it as a normal habit, most school days.
explain: Routinely can also mean often, as a habit, with no special reason. «Dad routinely walks the dog after tea.» He does not walk the dog because of anything special; it is simply what he does. Ask yourself: is this just what usually happens?
explain: Routinely can describe bad things too. «Cyclists are routinely ignored by drivers.» The word routinely tells you this keeps happening, again and again. The sentence is not good news, so the context shows that it is a bad thing.
fact: Routinely means as a normal, regular part of what happens, or usually.
fact: Routinely can also mean often, as a habit, without a special reason.
fact: «Doctors routinely check children's height.» This is a normal check they do.
fact: «Teachers routinely take the register.» Taking the register is a normal part of the school day.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping in usually or often: if the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
exercise: «Mum routinely packs my lunch on school days.» What does routinely mean here? | Once, by accident | Angrily | *As a normal, regular habit | Very quickly
exercise: «Cyclists are routinely ignored by drivers.» What does routinely tell us? | It happens only once, on a sunny day | It is a good thing that happens rarely | *It happens all the time, and it is a bad thing | It is a funny joke
exercise: Which word could replace routinely in «Teachers routinely take the register»? | Never | Suddenly | *Usually | Quietly
test: «Dad routinely walks the dog after tea, with no special reason.» What does routinely mean? | Angrily, after a fight | Only on his birthday | Very slowly | *Often, as a habit
test: «Doctors routinely check children's height at the clinic.» What does this sentence show? | It happens by chance, just once | It is a secret | It never happens | *It is a normal, regular check
exam: Priya says routinely means rarely. Is she right? | No, it means very loudly | Yes, it means never | Yes, it means rarely | *No, it means usually or often, as a normal habit
